.TH ZERODDS-GRPC-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-grpc-bridged \- DDS to gRPC bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-grpc-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-bind\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-reflection\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fIDDS:SVC\fR]...
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-grpc-bridged
exposes each mapped DDS topic as a gRPC service:
.B Publish
writes the
.I Sample
payload to the topic,
.B Subscribe
returns the next sample (one per call). The payload is opaque bytes, the
DDS user data as it is. TLS with ALPN
.IR h2 ,
mTLS, bearer and JWT authentication, a topic ACL and the reflection
service are served; the
.I grpc-timeout
header is not applied. Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-grpc-bridge-1.0.md .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
YAML config (Spec \(sc3). See
.BR zerodds-grpc-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-bind =\fIADDR\fR
HTTP/2 bind addr. Default:
.IR 0.0.0.0:50051 .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
TLS cert PEM.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
TLS key PEM.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-client\-ca =\fIFILE\fR
CA PEM for client certificates (mTLS).
.TP
.BR \-\-reflection
Enable the gRPC reflection service.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fIDDS:SVC\fR
Inline topic mapping override.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listen addr.
.PP
Test hooks. Real options, documented because the program accepts them
and an option nobody can find is one nobody maintains.
.TP
.BR \-\-once
Serve one request, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-idle\-timeout\-ms =\fIN\fR
Exit after \fIN\fR milliseconds without a request.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop the daemon.
SIGHUP reads the configuration again: the TLS certificate and key, the
auth settings and the topic ACL apply from then on (the certificate to new
connections). Changed binds, domain, topic mappings, reflection or TLS on
or off need a restart and are logged. A configuration that does not load
changes nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 normal stop, 1 configuration (also an auth mode that cannot be served,
such as
.B jwt
without
.BR auth.jwt.public_key ),
2 bind, 3 DDS, 4 TLS.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/grpc-bridged.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-grpc-bridged.yaml (5),
.BR grpcurl (1).
